--- str -- string utility functions for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `str` stdlib interface: 45 functions
--- covering basic transforms, case conversion, search, and string
--- transformation. The Rust bridge in `plugin-lib-utils` loads this file
--- via `include_str!`, parses the `cap` declarations for the plugin
--- capability surface, and registers the Rust handls (handlers) in an
--- `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native Rust string impl.
---
--- All 45 functions are FFI atoms (they call Rust `String`/`str` methods
--- that cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows without losing the exact
--- `TypeMismatch` error messages the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl`
--- declaration form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust
--- `Function` impls in `ops.rs` provide the logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- str.upper -- convert a string to uppercase.
--- str.lower -- convert a string to lowercase.
--- str.trim -- strip leading and trailing whitespace.
--- str.trim_start -- strip leading whitespace.
--- str.trim_end -- strip trailing whitespace.
--- str.trim_matches -- strip leading/trailing characters matching a set.
--- str.reverse -- reverse the characters of a string.
--- str.length -- count the characters in a string.
--- str.concat -- concatenate two or more strings.
--- str.is_empty -- test whether a string is empty.
--- str.equals -- test whether two strings are equal.
--- str.is_alpha -- test whether a string contains only alphabetic characters.
--- str.is_numeric -- test whether a string contains only numeric characters.
--- str.is_alphanumeric -- test whether a string contains only alphanumeric characters.
--- str.capitalize -- capitalize the first character of a string.
--- str.title_case -- capitalize the first character of each word.
--- str.snake_case -- convert a string to snake_case.
--- str.camel_case -- convert a string to camelCase.
--- str.pascal_case -- convert a string to PascalCase.
--- str.kebab_case -- convert a string to kebab-case.
--- str.contains -- test whether a string contains a substring.
--- str.starts_with -- test whether a string starts with a prefix.
--- str.ends_with -- test whether a string ends with a suffix.
--- str.count -- count non-overlapping occurrences of a substring.
--- str.find -- find the char index of the first occurrence of a substring.
--- str.rfind -- find the char index of the last occurrence of a substring.
--- str.levenshtein -- compute the Levenshtein edit distance between two strings.
--- str.similarity -- compute a normalized similarity ratio between two strings.
--- str.split -- split a string by a separator into a list.
--- str.join -- join a list of strings with a separator.
--- str.replace -- replace all occurrences of a substring.
--- str.replace_first -- replace the first occurrence of a substring.
--- str.repeat -- repeat a string a given number of times.
--- str.char_at -- get the character at a given index.
--- str.slice -- extract a substring by char-index range.
--- str.pad_left -- pad a string on the left to a target length.
--- str.pad_right -- pad a string on the right to a target length.
--- str.strip_prefix -- remove a leading prefix if present.
--- str.strip_suffix -- remove a trailing suffix if present.
--- str.lines -- split a string into a list of lines.
--- str.split_at -- split a string at a char index into two parts.
--- str.split_whitespace -- split a string on whitespace into a list.
--- str.truncate -- truncate a string to a max length with an optional suffix.
--- str.slugify -- convert a string to a URL-safe slug.
--- str.word_wrap -- wrap text to a given line width.
